# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before transpilation the CPC adds only a small, fixed number of gates over the bare payload. After transpilation to the backend, the overhead concentrates in the two-qubit layers.  The two-qubit gate count rises, and the two-qubit depth, a useful indicator of accumulated noise, also grows. Part of this overhead is routing. A single ancilla has to reach the supports of both $L$ and $R$, so even the weight-2 $R$ coupling can need extra gates, and this full-circuit count does not separate the two contributions.\n"
msgstr "Bago ang transpilation, maliit at fixed na bilang lang ng gate ang idinaragdag ng CPC sa payload. Pagkatapos ng transpilation sa backend, nakatuon ang overhead sa mga two-qubit layer.  Tumataas ang bilang ng two-qubit gate, at lumalaki rin ang two-qubit depth, isang kapaki-pakinabang na indikasyon ng naipong ingay. Bahagi ng overhead na ito ay routing. Kailangang maabot ng iisang ancilla ang mga support ng parehong $L$ at $R$, kaya kahit ang weight-2 na $R$ coupling ay maaaring mangailangan ng dagdag na gate, at hindi pinaghihiwalay ng bilang sa buong circuit na ito ang dalawang kontribusyon.\n"

